1. What is Golang (Go)?
========================
Go (Golang) is an open-source programming language created by Google engineers Robert Griesemer, Rob Pike, and Ken Thompson.

Its primary goals were:

➔ Simplicity
➔ High performance
➔ Concurrency (handling many requests simultaneously)
➔ Fast compilation
➔ Cloud-native development

Think of Go as:
Easy like Python, Fast like C/C++, Built for cloud applications

Why was Go created?
====================
Google had problems with: Huge codebases, Long compile times, Massive distributed systems
They wanted a language that: Builds quickly, Uses fewer resources, Runs efficiently, Handles thousands of concurrent requests. Thus "Go" was born.

2. Who uses Go?
================
Many cloud-native and DevOps tools are written in Go.
Examples: Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, Premetheus, Helm, Vault, Consul all these are written in Go.

3. Why is Go popular in Cloud and Microservices?
================================================
Suppose 10,000 users hit your application. Go uses lightweight threads called: Goroutines, instead of expensive OS threads.
This allows: High throughput, Low memory usage, and Fast response times
That's why Go is common for: APIs, Microservices, Cloud platforms, DevOps tools and Networking software

